Description: Grab, mark up and copy screenshots on GNOME
 GrabbyHands is a screenshot tool for the GNOME desktop on Wayland. Press
 Print Screen, drag over what you want, and copy, save, mark up or pin it
 in one click.
 .
  * Region, whole-screen and window capture, with a pixel magnifier and a
    delay timer
  * An editor with arrows, shapes, text, callouts, numbered steps, blur,
    pixelate, black-out, spotlight, magnify, stickers and crop
  * Copy text out of a screenshot (OCR) and read QR codes and barcodes
  * Auto-redact emails, phone numbers, card numbers and other personal
    details before sharing
  * Identify Color (HEX, RGB, CMYK), pinned screenshots and a capture
    history
 .
 Everything happens on your computer: GrabbyHands has no network access.
 .
 Text recognition needs tesseract-ocr and QR reading needs
 python3-zxing-cpp; both are recommended and installed by default. Without
 them those two features are hidden and everything else works.
 .
 This package also installs the "GrabbyHands Window Helper" GNOME Shell
 extension, which tells GrabbyHands where windows are so it can capture a
 single window and, if you ask for it in Settings, makes the screenshot
 button in GNOME's system menu start GrabbyHands. It is off until you turn
 it on.
